orthant 1 language

- # `↯/s.24.1` — `recover` argument must be match cases
+ # `↯/s.24.1` — el argumento de `recover` debe ser casos de coincidencia

- Raised at compiletime when the argument to `recover` is not written as a literal block of
- `case` clauses.
+ Se lanza en tiempo de compilación cuando el argumento de `recover` no está escrito como un bloque
+ literal de cláusulas `case`.

- ## Cause
+ ## Causa

- `recover` inspects the cases as the code compiles, so that it knows which error types are
- handled. A partial function computed elsewhere, or passed as a value, cannot be inspected.
+ `recover` inspecciona los casos al compilarse el código, para saber qué tipos de error se tratan.
+ Una función parcial calculada en otro sitio, o pasada como valor, no puede inspeccionarse.

- ## Example message
+ ## Mensaje de ejemplo

=
- ```
+ ```

- [↯/s.24.1] argument to `recover` should be a partial function implemented as match cases
+ [↯/s.24.1] argument to `recover` should be a partial function implemented as match cases

= [↯/s.24.1] argument to `recover` should be a partial function implemented as match cases
- ```
+ ```

- ## Resolution
+ ## Solución

- Write the cases inline:
+ Escribe los casos en línea:

- ```scala
+ ```scala

- def readConfiguration(): Text raises Io.Error = t"verbose = true"
+ def readConfiguration(): Text raises Io.Error = t"verbose = true"

- val fallback: Text = t""
+ val fallback: Text = t""

- recover:
+ recover:

-   case error: Io.Error => fallback
+   case error: Io.Error => fallback

- . protect(readConfiguration())
+ . protect(readConfiguration())

= . protect(readConfiguration())
- ```
+ ```

